 -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the data store. Constraints: o pattern: ([^\r\n])* WindowSize -&gt; (integer) The amount of time to spend processing each micro batch. Constraints: o min: 0 DetectSchema -&gt; (boolean) Whether to automatically determine the schema from the incoming data. Table -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the table in the database to read from. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* Database -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the database to read from. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* StreamingOptions -&gt; (structure) Specifies the streaming options. BootstrapServers -&gt; (string) A list of bootstrap server URLs, for example, as b-1.vpc-test-2.o4q88o.c6.kafka.us-east-1.amazon- aws.com:9094 . This option must be specified in the API call or defined in the table metadata in the Data Catalog. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* SecurityProtocol -&gt; (string) The protocol used to communicate with brokers. The possible values are "SSL" or "PLAINTEXT" . Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* ConnectionName -&gt; (string) The name of the connection. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* TopicName -&gt; (string) The topic name as specified in Apache Kafka. You must specify at least one of "topicName" , "as- sign" or "subscribePattern" . Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* Assign -&gt; (string) The specific TopicPartitions to consume. You must specify at least one of "topicName" , "assign" or "subscribePattern" . Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* SubscribePattern -&gt; (string) A Java regex string that identifies the topic list to subscribe to. You must specify at least one of "topicName" , "assign" or "subscribePattern" . Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* Classification -&gt; (string) An optional classification. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* Delimiter -&gt; (string) Specifies the delimiter character. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* StartingOffsets -&gt; (string) The starting position in the Kafka topic to read data from. The possible values are "earliest" or "latest" . The default value is "latest" . Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* EndingOffsets -&gt; (string) The end point when a batch query is ended. Possi- ble values are either "latest" or a JSON string that specifies an ending offset for each TopicPar- tition . Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* PollTimeoutMs -&gt; (long) The timeout in milliseconds to poll data from Kafka in Spark job executors. The default value is 512 . Constraints: o min: 0 NumRetries -&gt; (integer) The number of times to retry before failing to fetch Kafka offsets. The default value is 3 . Constraints: o min: 0 RetryIntervalMs -&gt; (long) The time in milliseconds to wait before retrying to fetch Kafka offsets. The default value is 10 . Constraints: o min: 0 MaxOffsetsPerTrigger -&gt; (long) The rate limit on the maximum number of offsets that are processed per trigger interval. The spec- ified total number of offsets is proportionally split across topicPartitions of different volumes. The default value is null, which means that the consumer reads all offsets until the known latest offset. Constraints: o min: 0 MinPartitions -&gt; (integer) The desired minimum number of partitions to read from Kafka. The default value is null, which means that the number of spark partitions is equal to the number of Kafka partitions. Constraints: o min: 0 IncludeHeaders -&gt; (boolean) Whether to include the Kafka headers. When the op- tion is set to "true", the data output will con- tain an additional column named "glue_stream- ing_kafka_headers" with type Array[Struct(key: String, value: String)] . The default value is "false". This option is available in Glue version 3.0 or later only. AddRecordTimestamp -&gt; (string) When this option is set to 'true', the data output will contain an additional column named "__src_timestamp" that indicates the time when the corresponding record received by the topic. The default value is 'false'. This option is supported in Glue version 4.0 or later. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* EmitConsumerLagMetrics -&gt; (string) When this option is set to 'true', for each batch, it will emit the metrics for the duration between the oldest record received by the topic and the time it arrives in Glue to CloudWatch. The met- ric's name is "glue.driver.streaming.maxConsumer- LagInMs". The default value is 'false'. This op- tion is supported in Glue version 4.0 or later. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* StartingTimestamp -&gt; (timestamp) The timestamp of the record in the Kafka topic to start reading data from. The possible values are a timestamp string in UTC format of the pattern yyyy-mm-ddTHH:MM:SSZ (where Z represents a UTC timezone offset with a +/-. For example: "2023-04-04T08:00:00+08:00"). Only one of StartingTimestamp or StartingOffsets must be set. DataPreviewOptions -&gt; (structure) Specifies options related to data preview for viewing a sample of your data. PollingTime -&gt; (long) The polling time in milliseconds. Constraints: o min: 10 RecordPollingLimit -&gt; (long) The limit to the number of records polled. Constraints: o min: 1 DropNullFields -&gt; (structure) Specifies a transform that removes columns from the dataset if all values in the column are 'null'. By de- fault, Glue Studio will recognize null objects, but some values such as empty strings, strings that are "null", -1 integers or other placeholders such as zeros, are not au- tomatically recognized as nulls. Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the transform node. Constraints: o pattern: ([^\r\n])* Inputs -&gt; (list) [required] The data inputs identified by their node names. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1 (string) Constraints: o pattern: [A-Za-z0-9_-]* NullCheckBoxList -&gt; (structure) A structure that represents whether certain values are recognized as null values for removal. IsEmpty -&gt; (boolean) Specifies that an empty string is considered as a null value. IsNullString -&gt; (boolean) Specifies that a value spelling out the word 'null' is considered as a null value. IsNegOne -&gt; (boolean) Specifies that an integer value of -1 is consid- ered as a null value. NullTextList -&gt; (list) A structure that specifies a list of NullValueField structures that represent a custom null value such as zero or other value being used as a null placeholder unique to the dataset. The DropNullFields transform removes custom null val- ues only if both the value of the null placeholder and the datatype match the data. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 50 (structure) Represents a custom null value such as a zeros or other value being used as a null placeholder unique to the dataset. Value -&gt; (string) [required] The value of the null placeholder. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* Datatype -&gt; (structure) [required] The datatype of the value. Id -&gt; (string) [required] The datatype of the value. Constraints: o pattern: [A-Za-z0-9_-]* Label -&gt; (string) [required] A label assigned to the datatype. Constraints: o pattern: [A-Za-z0-9_-]* Merge -&gt; (structure) Specifies a transform that merges a DynamicFrame with a staging DynamicFrame based on the specified primary keys to identify records. Duplicate records (records with the same primary keys) are not de-duplicated. Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the transform node. Constraints: o pattern: ([^\r\n])* Inputs -&gt; (list) [required] The data inputs identified by their node names. Constraints: o min: 2 o max: 2 (string) Constraints: o pattern: [A-Za-z0-9_-]* Source -&gt; (string) [required] The source DynamicFrame that will be merged with a staging DynamicFrame . Constraints: o pattern: [A-Za-z0-9_-]* PrimaryKeys -&gt; (list) [required] The list of primary key fields to match records from the source and staging dynamic frames. (list) (string) Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* Union -&gt; (structure) Specifies a transform that combines the rows from two or more datasets into a single result. Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the transform node. Constraints: o pattern: ([^\r\n])* Inputs -&gt; (list) [required] The node ID inputs to the transform. Constraints: o min: 2 o max: 2 (string) Constraints: o pattern: [A-Za-z0-9_-]* UnionType -&gt; (string) [required] Indicates the type of Union transform. Specify ALL to join all rows from data sources to the resulting DynamicFrame. The resulting union does not remove duplicate rows. Specify DISTINCT to remove duplicate rows in the re- sulting DynamicFrame. Possible values: o ALL o DISTINCT PIIDetection -&gt; (structure) Specifies a transform that identifies, removes or masks PII data. Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the transform node. Constraints: o pattern: ([^\r\n])* Inputs -&gt; (list) [required] The node ID inputs to the transform. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1 (string) Constraints: o pattern: [A-Za-z0-9_-]* PiiType -&gt; (string) [required] Indicates the type of PIIDetection transform. Possible values: o RowAudit o RowHashing o RowMasking o RowPartialMasking o ColumnAudit o ColumnHashing o ColumnMasking EntityTypesToDetect -&gt; (list) [required] Indicates the types of entities the PIIDetection transform will identify as PII data. PII type entities include: PERSON_NAME, DATE, USA_SNN, EMAIL, USA_ITIN, USA_PASSPORT_NUMBER, PHONE_NUMBER, BANK_ACCOUNT, IP_ADDRESS, MAC_ADDRESS, USA_CPT_CODE, USA_HCPCS_CODE, USA_NATIONAL_DRUG_CODE, USA_MEDICARE_BENEFICIARY_IDENTIFIER, USA_HEALTH_INSUR- ANCE_CLAIM_NUMBER,CREDIT_CARD,USA_NA- TIONAL_PROVIDER_IDENTIFIER,USA_DEA_NUMBER,USA_DRI- VING_LICENSE (string) Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* OutputColumnName -&gt; (string) Indicates the output column name that will contain any entity type detected in that row. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* SampleFraction -&gt; (double) Indicates the fraction of the data to sample when scanning for PII entities. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 1 ThresholdFraction -&gt; (double) Indicates the fraction of the data that must be met in order for a column to be identified as PII data. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 1 MaskValue -&gt; (string) Indicates the value that will replace the detected en- tity. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 256 o pattern: [*A-Za-z0-9_-]* RedactText -&gt; (string) Specifies whether to redact the detected PII text. When set to true , PII content is replaced with redac- tion characters. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* RedactChar -&gt; (string) The character used to replace detected PII content when redaction is enabled. The default redaction char- acter is * . Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* MatchPattern -&gt; (string) A regular expression pattern used to identify addi- tional PII content beyond the standard detection algo- rithms. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* NumLeftCharsToExclude -&gt; (integer) The number of characters to exclude from redaction on the left side of detected PII content. This allows preserving context around the sensitive data. Constraints: o min: 0 NumRightCharsToExclude -&gt; (integer) The number of characters to exclude from redaction on the right side of detected PII content. This allows preserving context around the sensitive data. Constraints: o min: 0 DetectionParameters -&gt; (string) Additional parameters for configuring PII detection behavior and sensitivity settings. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* DetectionSensitivity -&gt; (string) The sensitivity level for PII detection. Higher sensi- tivity levels detect more potential PII but may result in more false positives. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* Aggregate -&gt; (structure) Specifies a transform that groups rows by chosen fields and computes the aggregated value by specified function. Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the transform node. Constraints: o pattern: ([^\r\n])* Inputs -&gt; (list) [required] Specifies the fields and rows to use as inputs for the aggregate transform. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1 (string) Constraints: o pattern: [A-Za-z0-9_-]* Groups -&gt; (list) [required] Specifies the fields to group by. (list) (string) Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* Aggs -&gt; (list) [required] Specifies the aggregate functions to be performed on specified fields. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 30 (structure) Specifies the set of parameters needed to perform aggregation in the aggregate transform. Column -&gt; (list) [required] Specifies the column on the data set on which the aggregation function will be applied. (string) Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0