aints: o min: 0 o max: 1024 o pattern: [\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF\t]* Type -&gt; (string) The hive type for this column in the Glue Studio schema. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 131072 o pattern: [\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF\t]* GlueStudioType -&gt; (string) The data type of the column as defined in Glue Studio. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 131072 o pattern: [\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF\t]* DynamoDBELTConnectorSource -&gt; (structure) Specifies a DynamoDB ELT connector source for extracting data from DynamoDB tables. Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the DynamoDB ELT connector source. Constraints: o pattern: ([^\r\n])* ConnectionOptions -&gt; (structure) The connection options for the DynamoDB ELT connector source. DynamodbExport -&gt; (string) Specifies the export type for DynamoDB data ex- traction. This parameter determines how data is exported from the DynamoDB table during the ELT process. Possible values: o ddb o s3 DynamodbUnnestDDBJson -&gt; (boolean) A boolean value that specifies whether to unnest DynamoDB JSON format during data extraction. When set to true , the connector will flatten nested JSON structures from DynamoDB items. When set to false , the original DynamoDB JSON structure is preserved. DynamodbTableArn -&gt; (string) [required] The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the DynamoDB ta- ble to extract data from. This parameter specifies the source table for the ELT operation. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* DynamodbS3Bucket -&gt; (string) The name of the Amazon S3 bucket used for interme- diate storage during the DynamoDB ELT process. This bucket is used to temporarily store exported DynamoDB data before it is processed by the ELT job. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* DynamodbS3Prefix -&gt; (string) The S3 object key prefix for files stored 