leARN" . Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* AddRecordTimestamp -&gt; (string) When this option is set to 'true', the data output will contain an additional column named "__src_timestamp" that indicates the time when the corresponding record received by the stream. The default value is 'false'. This option is supported in Glue version 4.0 or later. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* EmitConsumerLagMetrics -&gt; (string) When this option is set to 'true', for each batch, it will emit the metrics for the duration between the oldest record received by the stream and the time it arrives in Glue to CloudWatch. The met- ric's name is "glue.driver.streaming.maxConsumer- LagInMs". The default value is 'false'. This op- tion is supported in Glue version 4.0 or later. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* StartingTimestamp -&gt; (timestamp) The timestamp of the record in the Kinesis data stream to start reading data from. The possible values are a timestamp string in UTC format of the pattern yyyy-mm-ddTHH:MM:SSZ (where Z represents a UTC timezone offset with a +/-. For example: "2023-04-04T08:00:00+08:00"). FanoutConsumerARN -&gt; (string) The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Kinesis Data Streams enhanced fan-out consumer. When specified, enables enhanced fan-out for dedicated throughput and lower latency data consumption. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* DataPreviewOptions -&gt; (structure) Additional options for data preview. PollingTime -&gt; (long) The polling time in milliseconds. Constraints: o min: 10 RecordPollingLimit -&gt; (long) The limit to the number of records polled. Constraints: o min: 1 CatalogKafkaSource -&gt; (structure) Specifies an Apache Kafka data store in the Data Catalog. Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the data store. Constraints: o pattern: ([^\r\n])* WindowSize -&gt; (integer) The amount of time to spend processing each micro batch. Constraints: o min: 0 DetectSchema -&gt; (boolean) Whether to automatically determine the schema from the incoming data. Table -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the table in the database to read from. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* Database -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the database to read from. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* StreamingOptions -&gt; (structure) Specifies the streaming options. BootstrapServers -&gt; (string) A list of bootstrap server URLs, for example, as b-1.vpc-test-2.o4q88o.c6.kafka.us-east-1.amazon- aws.com:9094 . This option must be specified in the API call or defined in the table metadata in the Data Catalog. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* SecurityProtocol -&gt; (string) The protocol used to communicate with brokers. The possible values are "SSL" or "PLAINTEXT" . Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* ConnectionName -&gt; (string) The name of the connection. Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* TopicName -&gt; (string) The topic name as specified in Apache Kafka. You must specify at least one of "topicName" , "as- sign" or "subscribePattern" . Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* Assign -&gt; (string) The specific TopicPartitions to consume. You must specify at least one of "topicName" , "assign" or "subscribePattern" . Constraints: o pattern: ([\u0009\u000B\u000C\u0020-\uD7FF\uE000-\uFFFD\uD800\uDC00-\uDBFF\uDFFF])* SubscribePattern -&gt; (string) A Java regex string that identifies the topic list to 